module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.Purity.KummerDivisorSection

/-!
# The Kummer class of the coordinate generates `R¹ j_* μ_N` at the origin of `𝔸¹_k`

Let `k` be a field, `N` invertible in `k` and `j : 𝐆_m ⟶ 𝐀¹_k` the punctured affine line. The
coordinate `t` is a local equation of the origin on all of `𝐀¹_k`, and its Kummer class
`∂ t ∈ Γ(𝐀¹_k, R¹ j_* μ_N)` (`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.Purity.localKummerClass`) generates the stalk
of `R¹ j_* μ_N` at every geometric point over the origin, freely over `ℤ/N`: the stalk is
`H¹` of the punctured strict henselisation, which is `ℤ/N` generated by the Kummer class of a
uniformiser.

This file states that fact as a proposition,
`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.Purity.AffineLineKummerGenerator k`: the input on `𝐀¹_k` from which the
generator property of the fundamental class of an étale divisor of a smooth relative curve is
transported by smooth base change (the base change maps commute with the Kummer coboundary,
`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.higherBaseChangeMapAb_comp_δ`). It is stated in the standard model of the
derived categories, in which that compatibility is proved.

The coboundary `∂` identifies `j_* 𝐆_m` with `R⁰ j_* 𝐆_m` through the degree-zero unit followed by
the comparison of the indexings of the right derived functors
(`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.Purity.kummerDirectImageδ_eq`), the normalisation in which the degree-zero
base change maps are the underived ones
(`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.map_rightDerivedZeroUnit_comp_higherBaseChangeMapAb_zero`).

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.Purity.AffineLineKummerGenerator`.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme
  TopologicalSpace Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.EtaleCohomology.Purity

section StandardModel

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

/-- **The Kummer class of the coordinate generates `R¹ j_* μ_N` at the origin, freely over
`ℤ/N`** (input A1c of relative purity): for every `N` invertible on `𝐆_m` and every geometric
point `x` of `𝐀¹_k` lying over the origin, `n ↦ n • (∂ t)_x` is a bijection from `ℤ/N` onto the
stalk of `R¹ j_* μ_N` at `x`. Stated in the standard model of the derived categories. -/
def AffineLineKummerGenerator (k : Type u) [Field k] : Prop :=
  ∀ (N : ℕ) (hN0 : N ≠ 0) (hN : IsUnit ((N : ℕ) : Γ((punctured k).toScheme, ⊤)))
    (ht : IsUnit (puncturedFunction (punctured k).ι ⊤ (coordinate k)))
    {Ω : Type u} [Field Ω] [IsSepClosed Ω] (x : Spec (.of Ω) ⟶ affineLine k),
    Set.range x.base ⊆ ((punctured k : Set (affineLine k)))ᶜ →
    ∀ y : (Scheme.pointSmallEtale x).fiber.obj ((opensToEtale (affineLine k)).obj ⊤),
      Function.Bijective (fun n : ZMod N => n.val •
        (Scheme.pointSmallEtale x).toPresheafFiber ((opensToEtale (affineLine k)).obj ⊤) y
          (kummerTarget (punctured k).ι N).obj
          (localKummerClass (punctured k).ι hN0 hN ⊤ (coordinate k) ht))

end StandardModel

end Stacks.EtaleCohomology.Purity

end
